{
  "$comment": [
    "Sending markets: the buckets a show announcement targets. NOT the same thing as src/data/cities,",
    "which is 307 SEO landing pages including Pune and Vilnius. A market is an audience we would actually",
    "mail about a show, so this list is short on purpose and every entry is edited by hand.",
    "",
    "WHY a separate file from src/data/cities: a city page exists to rank in Google, a market exists to",
    "address an audience, and the two sets are not the same shape. Merging them would mean either adding",
    "coordinates and alias lists to 307 SEO records, or letting any new SEO page silently become a",
    "sending bucket. citySlugs below is the explicit bridge, so events.ts citySlug values keep resolving.",
    "",
    "WHY the aliases are keyed by state: 'Arlington' is both Virginia and Texas, and 'Hollywood' is both",
    "Florida and a Los Angeles neighborhood. markets.test.ts asserts that any alias appearing under two",
    "markets is only ever reachable with a state, so a future edit cannot quietly create a coin flip.",
    "",
    "WHY stateRollup omits NY, NJ, CA, TX, FL, PA and VA: those states hold more than one market, so a",
    "bare state is not an answer. The listed states each contain exactly one market we mail."
  ],
